# Template for the gitignored `.env`. Copy it and fill in your own values:
#
#     cp .env.template .env
#
# Everything here is personal: each contributor uses their own DagsHub account
# and their own token, so a leaked or revoked token costs one person a minute,
# not the team a migration. `.env` is in `.gitignore` and stays there.
#
# `recommenditos/config.py` loads this repository's `.env` with python-dotenv at
# import time, so every pipeline stage, every test and every script sees these
# values without doing anything itself. It loads `<repo>/.env` by name and does
# not search upwards, so a clone nested inside another checkout gets its own
# credentials or none - never the other one's.
#
# Every variable here is read by the project, and nothing the project reads is
# missing. That is asserted by a test, because a template listing a variable
# nothing reads is how a contributor comes to believe that filling it in
# configures something.
#
# Full walkthrough from a fresh clone to a pulled dataset and a visible MLflow
# run: docs/docs/getting-started.md.

# --- DagsHub / MLflow -------------------------------------------------------
# One DagsHub repository is both our DVC remote and our MLflow tracking server:
# https://dagshub.com/recommenditos/MLOPS_Recommenditos (EDN-19).
#
# Where to get the token: sign in to DagsHub, open your avatar in the top right
# -> "Your Settings" -> "Tokens", and copy the "Default Access Token" (or create
# a new one). It is a password: it is not shown again after you leave the page on
# a freshly created token, and it grants everything your account can do.
#
# MLflow reads these three names from the environment itself. DagsHub's tracking
# server authenticates with HTTP basic auth and takes the token as the password,
# which is why the password below is a token and not your DagsHub password.
# `recommenditos/tracking.py` checks all three before a run starts.
#
# DVC needs the same account and the same token, and this file cannot give them
# to it: DVC's HTTP remote reads `user` and `password` from its own config and no
# environment variable at all. So the token is entered a second time, with
# `dvc remote modify origin --local`, into the gitignored `.dvc/config.local`.
# That is a property of DVC, not a choice, and there is deliberately no
# `DAGSHUB_USER_TOKEN` here: it would read as if filling it in configured DVC.
# See docs/docs/getting-started.md step 4.

# The `.mlflow` endpoint of the repository above. The same for everyone.
MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=https://dagshub.com/recommenditos/MLOPS_Recommenditos.mlflow
# Your DagsHub login name, not your e-mail address.
MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME=
# The access token from the page above.
MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD=
